# ShadCN UI Usage

This project uses **shadcn/ui** for all UI elements. Always prefer shadcn components over raw HTML elements or other UI libraries.

## Initialization

If shadcn is not yet initialized in the project, run:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest init
```

## Adding Components

If a particular shadcn component is not yet installed, add it using:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add <component-name>
```

### Examples

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
npx shadcn@latest add input
npx shadcn@latest add card
npx shadcn@latest add dialog
```

## Guidelines

- **Always** use shadcn components for UI elements (buttons, inputs, cards, dialogs, etc.)
- Components are located in `components/ui/` after installation
- Import components from `@/components/ui/<component-name>`
- Do **not** install or use other UI libraries (e.g. Material UI, Chakra UI) unless explicitly requested
- If a needed component doesn't exist in shadcn, build it using existing shadcn primitives and Tailwind CSS
